Z||000000||btoth||10-09-2001||02:06 PM||||When I accelerate slowly (like when I'm stuck behind a slow person  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">), my engine seems to lag or stutter.  But when I push the throttle further it'll go just fine.  The only thing that I could think would cause this would be the injectors.  If the throttle isn't open far enough it might not be getting enough gas... does that make sense?  If I do make sense, could just using some injector cleaner clear things up a bit or not?<P>Info - 86 GT, new long-block 2.8, new sensors, no vacuum leaks, new cat.  I never had the injectors replaced (which is why I suspect them).  94k mi.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||10-09-2001||02:41 PM||||did you clean the throtle position switch???<BR>both the inside throtle and the conections wires clips??.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cozmo||10-09-2001||04:15 PM||||Also take a look at the inside of the throttle body and the plate.  My '85 did the same thing, the throttle body had a ton of black crud all over the inside. Cleaned it up and it ran fine.<P><P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
